00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:49,220
Absolutely. You'll love the feeling. There's nothing like it.

267
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:54,300
Okay. Okay. So how should I do it?

268
00:14:54,510 --> 00:14:56,760
How about at a game on the big screen?

269
00:14:56,930 --> 00:15:00,480
Huh! How about at a Foot Locker?

270
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:05,650
What? What, he obviously thinks that's a nice way to be proposed to.

271
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:09,400
Plus, he'd never suspect it.

272
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:09,400
Yeah, that does make sense.

273
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:13,240
Okay, now, would you two like that?

274
00:15:09,570 --> 00:15:13,240
Sounds good to me.

275
00:15:13,410 --> 00:15:15,620
But what would a guy think?

276
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,660
Uh, Nana's on the phone.

277
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,660
Wow.

278
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:24,500
That's interesting, since she died seven years ago.

279
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:26,750
She did?

280
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,130
Who got her condo in Boca?

281
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,760
Hello?

282
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:34,680
It's our nanny.

283
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:36,260
Hi.

284
00:15:36,430 --> 00:15:41,140
Oh, God, I hope you feel better. Okay. Bye.

285
00:15:41,310 --> 00:15:43,060
That's Molly. She's sick.

286
00:15:43,230 --> 00:15:46,360
Can you watch Emma today?

287
00:15:43,230 --> 00:15:46,360
I can't. I have back-to-back classes.

288
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:49,530
Did Molly say what she had? Because my throat's been hurting.

289
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,530
Menstrual cramps.

290
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:55,820
I don't think that's what this is.

291
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:59,790
Can any of you watch Emma?

292
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:59,790
No, I'm sorry, sweetie.

293
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,830
No, I've got work, and then I'm proposing.

294
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,540
Great. Shoot. What am I gonna do?

295
00:16:05,710 --> 00:16:07,590
Well, I could do it.

296
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:11,210
Well, actually...

297
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:11,210
Can I talk to you for a second?

298
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:12,550
Yeah.

299
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,800
Um, I do not want her babysitting our child.

300
00:16:15,970 --> 00:16:19,560
Why not?

301
00:16:15,970 --> 00:16:19,560
For one thing, she keeps calling her Ella.

302
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:23,060
Ella's a nice name.

303
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:23,060
Fine, we'll call the next one Ella.

304
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:25,350
What, the next one?

305
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:25,350
Okay.

306
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:29,320
I don't want her watching our baby.

307
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:32,690
Ross, I am trying to help her become a better person.

308
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,780
This is a huge breakthrough for her.

309
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:39,200
She just offered to do something for another human being.

310
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:41,950
You know, I don't know

311
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:41,950
Ross, I'm telling you...

312
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:45,960
...she's giving up getting her eyebrows shaped to do this, all right?

313
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:49,840
Do you understand how important that is in our world?

314
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:56,180
Uh, listen, I couldn't help but overhear, because I was trying to.

315
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,680
Listen, let me do this. I really want to help you guys out.

316
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:04,060
And plus, Rachel's been so wonderful to me.

317
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:09,310
Absolutely.

318
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:09,310
Oh, great!

319
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,730
So how much does it pay?

320
00:17:18,070 --> 00:17:20,320
Hey, Joe. How's the second draft of the letter coming?

321
00:17:20,490 --> 00:17:23,830
Great. I'm finished. In fact, I just dropped it off at the agency.

322
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:27,920
You dropped it off?

323
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:27,920
Yeah.

324
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,080
Can we read it? Can you print out another copy?

325
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,050
No can do, amigo.

326
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:37,510
No, I didn't use the computer. It felt more personal to handwrite it.

327
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:40,430
You handwrote it?

328
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:40,430
Yeah, and don't worry.

329
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:43,100
I didn't try to sound smart at all.

330
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,520
See you later.

331
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:49,400
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. That letter is gonna go in our file.

332
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:51,400
We're never gonna get a kid.

333
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:53,780
We're gonna be one of those old couples...

334
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,280
...that collects orchids or has a lot of birds.

335
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:59,200
It's okay. It's okay. You know what?

336
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:02,780
I will just call the agency and tell them to throw out the letter.

337
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:04,490
Okay, good.

338
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:06,830
Hello, this is Chandler Bing.

339
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,290
Someone just dropped off a handwritten recommendation letter and...

340
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:15,340
Uh-huh.

341
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:17,590
Okay.

342
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:21,510
Thank you. Goodbye.

343
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,550
We're screwed, aren't we?

344
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:26,430
You know what? Just tell me on the way to the bird store.

345
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,440
They loved it.

346
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:29,440
What?

347
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:33,690
They thought it was very smart of us to have a child write the recommendation letter.

348
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:36,820
They thought Joey was a child?

349
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:40,030
She guessed 8, 9, based on his drawings.

350
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,700
Hi.

351
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,700
What'd you guys do today?

352
00:18:45,870 --> 00:18:51,000
Ella wanted to go out, so we went shopping and got some sushi.

353
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:54,590
That sounds like fun.

354
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:54,590
Yeah, not really.

355
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:56,300
Babies are dull.

356
00:18:58,010 --> 00:19:01,930
Hey. Hi, how's my girl?

357
00:18:58,010 --> 00:19:01,930
I'm fine.

358
00:19:02,890 --> 00:19:06,600
And I got you a present for letting me stay with you.

359
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,850
Ready?

360
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,850
Yeah.

361
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,020
Ta-da!

362
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:15,820
You pierced her ears?

363
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,860
Doesn't it make her nose look smaller?

364
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,780
You pierced her ears?

365
00:19:26,990 --> 00:19:29,370
How could you do this without telling me?

366
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:33,250
If I had told you, then it wouldn't have been a surprise, now would it?

367
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,170
I think she looks cute.

368
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,130
But I am wrong.

369
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:43,340
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Here comes Ross. He's gonna flip out.

370
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,100
Why, did something happen to his falafel cart?

371
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:49,180
Hey, guys.

372
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:49,180
Ross!

373
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:53,270
Hi, Emma. Oh. Why is she wearing her hat so low?

374
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:56,400
She can barely see.

375
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:56,400
I don't really want her to see.

376
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,360
Why not?

377
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:02,200
Because there are so many terrible sights in this world.

378
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:05,740
Like war. Or that thing in Joey's refrigerator. Remember?

379
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:08,990
It was in a milk carton, but it looked like meat?

380
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,790
Come here. Come here.

381
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,330
There she is. Hi.

382
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:20,050
What?

383
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:20,050
Nothing.

384
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:22,800
Hi.

385
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,890
What...?

386
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:40,900
Please tell me those are clip-ons!

387
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:40,900
Oh, they're real.

388
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,610
Did she do this to her?

389
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:46,240
I told you we shouldn't have left Emma with her!

390
00:20:46,410 --> 00:20:48,370
I know. And you were right, Ross.

391
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:52,160
Okay? You are so irresponsible! I am never letting you babysit again!

392
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:54,290
You know what? This kid needs me, okay?

393
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:58,330
She needs to have a cool, fun aunt.

394
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:58,330
I'm a cool, fun aunt.

395
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,290
Okay.

396
00:21:00,670 --> 00:21:06,260
Hey! Monica can be cool and fun at organized indoor projects.

397
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:11,600
All I wanted to do was help you try to figure out what to do with your life.

398
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:13,060
This is how you repay me?

399
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:16,980
I don't need you to help me. I already know what I'm gonna do with my life.

400
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:20,650
Oh, yeah? Since when?

401
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:20,650
Since today.

402
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:26,030
I am going to be a baby stylist.

403
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:30,370
What?

404
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:30,370
That's not a thing!

405
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:32,990
Well, it should be.

406
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,960
I'm gonna help babies learn how to accessorize...

407
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:39,500
...what colors to wear, what clothes are slimming.

408
00:21:39,710 --> 00:21:43,840
Babies don't care if they're slim!

409
00:21:39,710 --> 00:21:43,840
Enter Amy.

410
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:48,130
Amy, I... I just... I just wanna...

411
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:48,130
What? What are you gonna do?

412
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:52,760
No more falafel for you!

413
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:07,360
Great game, huh?

414
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:07,360
Uh-huh.

415
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:13,990
Why do you keep looking at the screen?

416
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:13,990
I'm not. I'm praying.

417
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:16,370
Please let the Knicks win.

418
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:18,710
Thank you, Thor.

419
00:22:19,790 --> 00:22:22,420
Where are you going?

420
00:22:19,790 --> 00:22:22,420
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

421
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:24,750
Well, I think you should wait.

422
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:24,750
Why?

423
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:30,380
Well, if you don't hold it in, you don't get all the nutrients.

424
00:22:31,010 --> 00:22:34,720
ANNOUNCER Please turn your attention to the big screen on the scoreboard.

425
00:22:35,430 --> 00:22:38,930
Someone has a special question to ask.

426
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:44,320
Mike Hannigan, will you marry me?

427
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:49,570
Get a load of this. She's proposing to him!

428
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:53,370
Guess we know who wears the pants in that family.

429
00:22:53,530 --> 00:22:56,160
Well, that's not very enlightened.

430
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:59,960
Hey! Hey!

431
00:23:00,250 --> 00:23:03,330
Boo us? Boo you!

432
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:13,090
Hello? Yeah, this is Joey Tribbiani.

433
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:15,180
Oh, hi.

434
00:23:16,890 --> 00:23:19,350
Well, I'm glad you liked my letter.

435
00:23:20,770 --> 00:23:24,400
No, my mommy and daddy aren't home right now.

436
00:23:25,690 --> 00:23:27,940
Okay, bye-bye.

437
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:32,910
She was nice.

438
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:36,490
Joey, get Amy's bags. She is moving out.

439
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:37,990
Woo-hoo!

440
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:42,790
You're kicking me out?

441
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:42,790
You put holes in my baby's ears.

442
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:45,170
At least now people will know she's a girl!

443
00:23:47,670 --> 00:23:50,300
I can't believe I ever even tried to help you.

444
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:53,050
You are so beyond help!

445
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:53,050
You know what?

446
00:23:53,260 --> 00:23:56,220
Ever since I got here, you have been nothing but negative.

447
00:23:56,430 --> 00:23:58,060
Excuse me?

448
00:23:56,430 --> 00:23:58,060
You didn't want me...

449
00:23:58,220 --> 00:24:00,600
...to marry the old guy with the great apartment.

450
00:24:00,770 --> 00:24:05,560
Then I tried to help your daughter de-emphasize her flaws...

451
00:24:05,730 --> 00:24:07,820
...and suddenly I'm the bad guy?

452
00:24:08,020 --> 00:24:11,900
Joey, where are those bags?

453
00:24:08,020 --> 00:24:11,900
She has a lot of crap!

454
00:24:12,650 --> 00:24:15,990
You know? When I moved in here, I thought, "This will be so great.

455
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:19,240
Just us sisters back together again like when we were kids."

456
00:24:19,410 --> 00:24:22,410
Except without that stupid Jill. Oh.

457
00:24:22,580 --> 00:24:24,870
Who has gotten fat, by the way.

458
00:24:26,790 --> 00:24:28,090
Seriously?

459
00:24:28,630 --> 00:24:30,840
Mom said she gained, like, 15 pounds.

460
00:24:31,050 --> 00:24:33,840
Hips or thighs?

461
00:24:31,050 --> 00:24:33,840
Ass and face.

462
00:24:35,260 --> 00:24:38,050
Oh, my God! I thought she was on Atkins.

463
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:40,220
She was. Carbs found her.

464
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:47,270
See? This is what I wanted.

465
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:51,030
Two sisters talking about real stuff.

466
00:24:53,610 --> 00:24:55,610
Oh, I can give you that.

467
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,160
You can?

468
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,160
Yeah.

469
00:24:58,370 --> 00:25:01,240
I kept trying to make you a better person, but you're...

470
00:25:01,410 --> 00:25:04,750
You're already a pretty perfect version of what you are.

471
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:07,750
Thank you.

472
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:10,590
You gotta admit, Emma does look cute.

473
00:25:12,210 --> 00:25:15,720
Did you just say, "Emma"?

474
00:25:12,210 --> 00:25:15,720
Oh, I'm sorry. Ella.

475
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:25,140
That woman didn't know what she was talking about, Mike.

476
00:25:25,310 --> 00:25:27,650
Obviously, you have balls.

477
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:31,860
Please, let's just forget the whole thing.

478
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:31,860
I would love it.

479
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,940
Consider it forgotten.

480
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,940
Thank you.

481
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:36,450
But just so you know...

482
00:25:36,610 --> 00:25:42,240
However and whenever you decide to propose, I promise I'll say yes.

483
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:44,910
Whether, you know, it's at a basketball game...

484
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:47,000
...or in skywriting...

485
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:49,880
...or, you know, like some lame guy in a cheesy movie...

486
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:52,090
...who hides it in the cake.

487
00:25:57,590 --> 00:26:00,300
It's in the cake, isn't it?

488
00:26:01,390 --> 00:26:04,890
Where else would lame Mr. No-Balls hide it?

489
00:26:05,060 --> 00:26:07,890
What's the matter with me? Why do I keep ruining this?

490
00:26:08,060 --> 00:26:10,480
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

491
00:26:08,060 --> 00:26:10,480
No, it's my fault.

492
00:26:10,690 --> 00:26:13,190
I keep trying to propose in these stupid ways...

493
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:17,570
...and I just wanna tell you I love you, and I wanna spend my life with you...

494
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:25,200
I'm gonna do this now.

495
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:25,200
Oh, my God.

496
00:26:28,750 --> 00:26:30,830
Phoebe, I...

497
00:26:28,750 --> 00:26:30,830
Wait. Oh, wait.

498
00:26:35,340 --> 00:26:37,050
Oh, no.

499
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:43,220
Ready?

500
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:43,220
Uh-huh.

501
00:26:43,390 --> 00:26:44,810
Okay.

502
00:26:47,390 --> 00:26:50,100
Phoebe, I love you.

503
00:26:51,690 --> 00:26:55,150
There's no one else in the world I would ask to marry me three times.

504
00:26:57,650 --> 00:27:00,070
But I want to take care of you...

505
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,660
...have babies with you...

506
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,240
...and grow old with you.

507
00:27:07,330 --> 00:27:10,370
Phoebe Buffay, will you marry me?

508
00:27:11,420 --> 00:27:13,170
Yes.

509
00:27:19,670 --> 00:27:22,180
I love you.

510
00:27:19,670 --> 00:27:22,180
I love you more.

511
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:23,550
Not possible.

512
00:27:33,060 --> 00:27:35,560
She's gonna be Mrs. No-Balls!

513
00:27:41,490 --> 00:27:44,700
So how's the, uh, baby-styling business going?

514
00:27:44,870 --> 00:27:46,990
Not that great.

515
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:51,040
It's almost as if people don't want to hear that their babies are ugly.

516
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:54,710
That's shocking.

517
00:27:55,790 --> 00:27:58,750
There's Ross. Hey, Ross.

518
00:28:00,300 --> 00:28:02,800
Hello, Ross?

519
00:28:04,510 --> 00:28:06,100
He's rude.

